### Explanation:
This is a complete, compilable C program that reads the analog voltage from a Honeywell MICROpeL MP-741 Combustible Gas Sensor via an MCP3008 ADC connected over SPI (CE0, channel 0), using the pigpio library at 1 MHz SPI clock, reading MCP3008 channel 0 in single-ended mode. The program converts the 10-bit ADC value to voltage using VREF = 3.3 V, then calculates PPM using the placeholder linear relationship PPM = voltage * 1000.0 (no actual calibration). The program logs the timestamp, voltage, and PPM to 'gas_log.txt' in append mode, and prints the voltage and PPM to the console every second.

The program checks SPI initialization, SPI transfer failures, and file open errors; on ADC read failure, it retries after a 100 ms delay. It uses a signal handler (SIGINT) to close SPI and terminate pigpio cleanly, with proper resource cleanup on all exit paths.

The program simulates a propane leak detector with continuous operation until Ctrl+C.

