# Raspberry Pi

## What is Raspberry Pi?
Raspberry Pi is a series of credit card-sized single-board computers developed in the United Kingdom by the Raspberry Pi Foundation to promote the teaching of basic computer science in schools and developing countries.

## What is the Raspberry Pi Foundation?
The Raspberry Pi Foundation is a UK-based charity that supports the Raspberry Pi project. It was founded in 2012 by , , and . The foundation's mission is to promote the use of the Raspberry Pi computer in education and to support the development of the Raspberry Pi hardware and software.

## What is the Raspberry Pi OS?
Raspberry Pi OS is the official operating system for the Raspberry Pi. It is based on Debian and includes a graphical user interface (GUI) and a set of pre-installed applications. Raspberry Pi OS is available in two versions: Raspberry Pi OS Lite (headless) and Raspberry Pi OS with desktop.

