### Explanation:
This is a complete, compilable C program that reads the moisture level from the YL-69 soil moisture sensor using the MCP3008 ADC over SPI channel 0, CE0, at a 1 MHz baud rate, with the sensor on MCP3008 single-ended channel 0. The program uses the pigpio library to initialize pigpio, open SPI, and read the ADC value. It also uses the pigpio library to close SPI and terminate pigpio on cleanup.

The program defines constants SPI_CHANNEL (0), SPI_BAUD (1000000), MCP3008_CHANNEL (0), READ_DELAY (60), MIN_ADC (300), MAX_ADC (800), and LOG_FILE ("soil_moisture_log.csv").

The program includes the headers pigpio.h, stdio.h, stdlib.h, unistd.h, time.h, signal.h, and string.h.

The program implements functions read_mcp3008(int channel), calculate_moisture_level(int adc_value), log_data(double moisture_level), signal_handler(int signal), and spi_setup(spi_config_t config).

The program reads the ADC value from the MCP3008 ADC over SPI channel 0, CE0, at a 1 MHz baud rate, with the sensor on MCP3008 single-ended channel 0. It uses the SPI command format: start bit 0x01, then a single-ended-plus-channel-select byte 0x80 | (channel << 4), then a dummy byte 0x00, reading the 10-bit ADC value as ((rx_buf[1] & 0x03) << 8) | rx_buf[2].

