### Explanation:
The program uses the pigpio library to interface with the VL53L0X sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x29. It configures GPIO 17 (BCM numbering) with a pull-up and triggers a single distance measurement on each falling edge detected there. It verifies sensor presence at 0x29 before initialization. To range, it writes 0x01 to SYSRANGE_START (register 0x00), polls bit 0 of RESULT_INTERRUPT_STATUS (register 0x13) until it sets, with a timeout of about 100 ms, then reads the 14-byte result block starting at RESULT_RANGE_STATUS (register 0x14) and extracts the 16-bit distance from bytes 10-11, and finally clears the interrupt by writing 0x01 to SYSTEM_INTERRUPT_CLEAR (register 0x0B). It applies robust error handling to every I2C transaction and to sensor-absent and timeout paths. It logs each timestamped distance measurement, in millimetres, to 'distance_log.txt' in CSV format as 'timestamp,distance_mm'. It handles SIGINT for graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle and log file and releasing pigpio resources on all exit paths.

### Notes:
- The program uses the pigpio library to interface with the VL53L0X sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x29.
- It configures GPIO 17 (BCM numbering) with a pull-up and triggers a single distance measurement on each falling edge detected there.
- It verifies sensor presence at 0x29 before initialization.
- To range, it writes 0x01 to SYSRANGE_START (register 0x00), polls bit 0 of RESULT_INTERRUPT_STATUS (register 0x13) until it sets, with a timeout of about 100 ms, then reads the 14-byte result block starting at RESULT_RANGE_STATUS (register 0x14) and extracts the 16-bit distance from bytes 10-11, and finally clears the interrupt by writing 0x01 to SYSTEM_INTERRUPT_CLEAR (register 0x0B).
- It applies robust error handling to every I2C transaction and to sensor-absent and timeout paths.
- It logs each timestamped distance measurement, in millimetres, to 'distance_log.txt' in CSV format as 'timestamp,distance_mm'.
- It handles SIGINT for graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle and log file and releasing pigpio resources on all exit paths.

