### Explanation:
This program uses the pigpio library to interface with two TCRT5000 IR reflective sensors on GPIO 17 and GPIO 18 (BCM numbering) to detect object proximity. It logs the readings (0 or 1) with a timestamp to 'obstacle_log.txt' every 100 milliseconds.

The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown and ensures all resources are properly released on exit. If a sensor read fails, it logs a clear error message to stderr and continues polling rather than terminating the program, and ensures all GPIO and file resources are released on every exit path, including SIGINT.

The program uses robust error handling for GPIO setup failures. If a sensor read fails, it logs an error message to stderr and continues rather than stopping.

The program uses the time.h library to get the current time and the localtime() function to convert it to a human-readable format. The strftime() function is used to format the time string in the desired format.

The program uses the fprintf() function to write the time string, sensor values, and a newline character to the log file.

The program uses the sleep() function to pause the program for 100 milliseconds before reading the sensors again.

The program uses the signal() function to register a signal handler for SIGINT. The sigint_handler() function is called when SIGINT is received. It closes the log file, terminates the GPIO library, and exits the program.

The program uses the gpioInitialise() function to initialize the GPIO library. If the initialization fails, it prints an error message and returns 1.

The program uses the gpioSetMode() function to set the GPIO modes for SENSOR_1 and SENSOR_2 to PI_INPUT.

The program uses the fopen() function to open the log file in write mode. If the file cannot be opened, it prints an error message and returns 1.

The program uses the gpioRead() function to read the sensor values. If the sensor read fails, it prints an error message and continues polling.

The program uses the time() and localtime() functions to get the current time and the strftime() function to format the time string in the desired format.

The program uses the fprintf() function to write the time string, sensor values, and a newline character to the log file.

The program uses the sleep() function to pause the program for 100 milliseconds before reading the sensors again.

The program uses the signal() function to register a signal handler for SIGINT. The sigint_handler() function is called when SIGINT is received. It closes the log file, terminates the GPIO library, and exits the program.

The program uses the gpioTerminate() function to terminate the GPIO library.

The program returns 0 to indicate successful execution.

