This program demonstrates how to use the pigpio library to interface with two TCRT5000 IR reflective sensors on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to detect object proximity, log the readings with a timestamp to a file, handle SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown, and ensure all resources are properly released on exit. It also demonstrates robust error handling for GPIO setup failures and graceful handling of sensor read failures.

