This is a complete, compilable C program that uses the pigpio library to interface two TCRT5000 IR obstacle avoidance sensors on GPIO 17 and GPIO 27. The program polls both sensors every 10 ms with a 50 ms software debounce per sensor, and logs every state transition with an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp, the sensor ID (1 or 2), and the event type ('DETECTED' for a HIGH-to-LOW transition, 'CLEARED' for LOW-to-HIGH) to 'proximity_log.txt'.

The program checks the return values of gpioInitialise(), gpioSetMode(), gpioRead(), and all file I/O operations. It ensures clean resource release, closing the log file and calling gpioTerminate(), on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

The program uses a simple state machine to debounce the sensor readings. It keeps track of the last state of each sensor and the number of consecutive readings that match the last state. When the number of consecutive readings reaches the debounce threshold, the program logs the event and updates the last state of the sensor.

The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to gracefully terminate the program and release resources.

This program is a good example of how to use the pigpio library to interface with sensors and log events to a file. It demonstrates the importance of checking return values, handling errors, and releasing resources on all exit paths.

