### Explanation:
This is a complete, compilable C program that uses the libgpiod library to measure distance with an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor. The program opens the GPIO chip, requests the trigger line as output, and the echo line as input. It then opens the log file and sets up the SIGINT handler.

The main loop of the program waits for the echo rising edge with a 30 ms timeout, then measures the echo pulse width with a 30 ms timeout, computing distance as (pulse_us * 0.0343) / 2.0 cm using a speed of sound of about 343 m/s at 20 degrees C. The program rejects readings outside 2-400 cm and logs an error line instead. It handles sensor-absent (echo never rises) and timeout paths explicitly. Every second, it logs the reading with an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp to 'distance_log.txt', flushing the file after each write.

The program installs a SIGINT handler that sets a volatile sig_atomic_t flag; on SIGINT, it releases all libgpiod resources, closes the log file, and exits cleanly. It uses libgpiod bulk or per-line requests and does not leak resources on any exit path.

