# Embedded C Developer

## Introduction

This repository contains my solutions to the Embedded C Developer challenge. The challenge is to write a C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B that uses the pigpio library to interface with a Silicon Labs Si7005 I2C humidity and temperature sensor at I2C bus 1, address 0x40, logging readings to the console every 2 seconds.

## Solution

The solution is provided in the `solution.c` file. It uses the pigpio library to interface with the I2C bus and the Si7005 sensor. The program opens the I2C bus and sets the CONFIG register to disable the heater. It then enters a loop that reads the temperature and humidity registers, converts the raw values to temperature and humidity, and prints the results to the console. The program handles SIGINT to gracefully exit and close the I2C handle and terminate pigpio.

## Usage

To run the solution, you need to have the pigpio library installed on your Raspberry Pi. You can follow the instructions on the pigpio website to install it: https://abyz.me.uk/rpi/pigpio/download.html.

Once the library is installed, you can compile and run the solution by running the following commands:

```
gcc -o solution solution.c -lpigpio
sudo ./solution
```

