### Explanation:
The program uses the libgpiod library to access the GPIO line and the I2C bus. The I2C bus is opened in read/write mode and the I2C address is set using the ioctl() system call. The sensor is initialized by sending the initialization command (0xBE 0x08 0x00) to the sensor. The relay is initialized by requesting an output line on the GPIO chip and setting the active state to high.

The main loop of the program reads the humidity from the sensor by sending the measurement command (0xAC 0x33 0x00) and reading 6 bytes of data. The status byte is checked to ensure the sensor is calibrated and not busy. The humidity is calculated from the remaining 5 bytes of data. The humidity is logged to the console with a timestamp. The relay is set to active if the humidity exceeds 60% and inactive if it is below 55%.

If an error occurs during any of these steps, the program retries up to 3 times with a 10 ms delay between retries. If all retries fail, an error is printed to stderr and the loop continues. If the SIGINT or SIGTERM signal is received, the GPIO line and I2C file descriptor are released and the program exits with code 0.

This program demonstrates the use of modern libraries, error handling, and resource management in embedded C development for Raspberry Pi.

