### Explanation:
This is a complete C program that reads the values of the 3-Way Tracing Sensor and prints them to the console every 50 ms. It uses the pigpio library to initialize the GPIOs and read their values. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown.

The program first initializes pigpio using gpioInitialise(). If the initialization fails, it prints an error message and exits with a non-zero status.

Next, it sets the modes of the three GPIOs using gpioSetMode(). If any of the mode setting fails, it prints an error message and terminates pigpio before exiting.

The program then sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM using signal(). The intHandler() function sets keepRunning to 0, which causes the main loop to exit.

The main loop reads the values of the three GPIOs using gpioRead() and prints them to the console in the specified format. It uses usleep(50000) to sleep for 50 ms between each iteration.

Finally, the program terminates pigpio using gpioTerminate() before exiting.

This program demonstrates the use of pigpio library to read digital inputs from a 3-Way Tracing Sensor and printing their values to the console. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown.

