This is a complete, compilable C program that uses the pigpio library to read heart-rate data from a Silicon Labs Si1182-A-GM optical heart-rate sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x4A. It initializes pigpio and opens the I2C bus, checking every return code. It verifies the sensor's PART_ID register (0x00) reads 0x02 and HW_REV register (0x01) reads 0x01, aborting with a clear error if the sensor is absent or wrong. It configures the sensor by writing the LED current (0x3F), averaging (0x04), and enable (0x01) registers, checking each write. It reads the 16-bit heart-rate register (0x2A) once per second using i2cReadWordData and converts the raw value to BPM using raw * 0.5. It applies a 5-sample moving average and validates that the filtered BPM is between 30 and 220 before logging. It appends valid readings as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS,BPM' to heart_rate.csv with an immediate flush. It retries on transient I2C read errors without crashing, and implements robust error handling for sensor-absent and bus-error conditions throughout. It handles SIGINT gracefully, closing the I2C handle, terminating pigpio, and closing the log file on all exit paths.

