### Explanation:
This program uses the libgpiod library to monitor a Keyes KY-026 flame sensor connected to GPIO17 (Broadcom pin 17, physical pin 11) on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. The sensor's DO pin is active-low, so it reads LOW when flame is detected and HIGH when clear. The program configures the line as input with an internal pull-up and polls it every 100 ms. When a falling edge is detected (HIGH-to-LOW transition, edge-triggered rather than level-triggered, to avoid duplicate alerts while the signal remains LOW), it prints 'FLAME DETECTED' to the console and appends a line with the current timestamp and 'FLAME DETECTED' to 'flame_log.txt' in append mode, flushing immediately.

The program checks every libgpiod call and file operation, and handles the case where the GPIO chip or line is unavailable. It installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler for graceful shutdown that releases the GPIO line, closes the chip, and closes the log file on all exit paths.

