### Explanation:
The program uses the pigpio library to communicate with the GY-50 L3G4200D gyroscope over I2C bus 1 at address 0x69. The program configures the sensor for normal mode with all axes enabled (CTRL_REG1 = 0x0F) and +-250 dps full-scale range (CTRL_REG4 = 0x00). The program reads all 6 data bytes starting at OUT_X_L (0x28) in a single block read, and converts raw values to degrees per second using sensitivity 8.75 mdps/LSB (i.e., divide by 114.285). The program logs each sample with a nanosecond-precision timestamp to 'gyro_log.csv' with a header row 'Timestamp,X,Y,Z', sampling every 10 ms. The program retries I2C writes up to 3 times during initialization, checks every I2C call, verifies the WHO_AM_I register (0x0F) reads 0xD3 before proceeding, and handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths. The program uses signal handling for graceful termination, performing clean resource release on SIGINT by closing the I2C handle, closing the file, and calling gpioTerminate().

