This is a complete, compilable C program that interfaces with an LSM303DLHC magnetometer via I2C bus 1 at default address 0x1E, connected to the physical SDA1/SCL1 pins, and controls an LED on GPIO17. It uses libgpiod for GPIO/PWM control and the standard Linux I2C interface (/dev/i2c-1, ioctl) for sensor communication, not wiringPi.

The program initializes the magnetometer by writing 0x18 to CTRL_REG1_M (0x20) for 10 Hz continuous conversion, and reads 6 bytes of data starting from OUT_X_L_M (0x08) in a single I2C block read. It then parses the magnetometer data, computes the magnitude of the Z-axis field, and adjusts the LED brightness proportionally using hardware PWM, sampling every 100 ms in the main loop.

The program handles I2C errors (e.g., sensor absent, bus errors) gracefully by logging the error and skipping the sample without crashing, and implements clean resource release on SIGINT/SIGTERM by releasing the PWM, closing the I2C file descriptor, and closing any log files.

This program is a complete solution to the problem, and it should compile and run correctly on a Raspberry Pi Zero W.

