### Explanation:

The program opens the I2C bus and verifies the WHO_AM_I register. It then configures the accelerometer for 50 Hz ODR with all axes enabled, full-scale +-2g, and a threshold interrupt on any-axis-high event with threshold 2000 mg and duration 0. It uses a 6-byte multi-byte burst read from OUT_X_L_A with auto-increment.

The program polls acceleration at roughly 10 ms intervals and stores each sample in a 64-entry in-memory circular buffer. On a rising edge of the INT1 GPIO interrupt, it prints a timestamp and dumps the last 10 buffered samples.

The program checks every I2C read/write and file-open call, printing a diagnostic to stderr and exiting non-zero on initialization failure. If a runtime I2C read fails, it prints a warning to stderr and skips that sample without corrupting the buffer.

The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl-C) gracefully by disabling the accelerometer, closing the I2C file descriptor, and exiting cleanly.

The program compiles with: gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o lsm303d_mon lsm303d_mon.c -lgpiod.

