### Explanation:
This program implements a simple I2C communication with an MPU-6050 gyroscope using the Linux I2C user-space API. It initializes the sensor by waking it up and verifies the device by reading the WHO_AM_I register. It then reads the gyroscope data registers starting at GYRO_XOUT_H for all 6 bytes, using a gyroscope sensitivity of 131.0 LSB/(deg/s) for the default +-250 dps range. It logs the data to a 100-sample in-memory circular buffer. It triggers a user-defined callback function when the absolute angular velocity (the magnitude of the X, Y, Z vector) exceeds a threshold of 50.0 degrees/second. It implements robust error handling for I2C communication failures and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown on SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

