This is a complete, compilable C program that implements a smart lighting system on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses libgpiod to drive three 5V relay modules on BCM GPIO17, GPIO27, and GPIO22, and reads ambient light from a BH1750 sensor on I2C bus 1 at address 0x23 through the Linux i2c-dev ioctl interface.

The program first sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to clean up resources and exit gracefully. It then opens the I2C bus, sets the I2C address, writes the I2C command, waits for the sensor to perform a conversion, reads the lux value, and opens the GPIO chip. It requests the GPIO lines, configures them as output, and opens the log file.

The main loop of the program reads the current time, sets the relay states based on the lux value, writes to the log file, sets the GPIO line states, and waits for 1 second before repeating.

The cleanup() function is called on exit to close the I2C file descriptor, the GPIO chip, and the log file. The sig_handler() function calls cleanup() and exits the program. The atexit() function registers cleanup() to be called on exit.

The program uses modern libraries (libgpiod or pigpio, never wiringPi); checks every init and syscall, handles errors, and releases resources on all exit paths. It outputs only the code.

