This program uses the Linux I2C-dev interface to communicate with the LSM303DLHC magnetometer over I2C. The I2C bus is opened in read/write mode, and the I2C slave address is set using the ioctl() function. The magnetometer is configured by writing to the MR_REG_M (0x02) and CRA_REG_M (0x00) registers. The X, Y, and Z values are read from the OUT_X_H_M (0x03), OUT_Y_H_M (0x07), and OUT_Z_H_M (0x05) registers, and the hard-iron calibration offsets are applied. The heading is computed using atan2f() and mapped to one of eight compass directions. The current time is obtained using the time() and localtime() functions, and the data is written to the CSV file using the fprintf() function. The program installs a signal handler for SIGINT to clean up resources and exit gracefully.

