### Explanation:
The program uses the pigpio library to read accelerometer data from an Analog Devices ADXL345 over I2C at address 0x53. The sensor is configured for ±2g range with full resolution by writing 0x0B to the DATA_FORMAT register (0x31), and measurement mode is enabled by writing 0x08 to the POWER_CTL register (0x2D). The program reads 6 bytes starting from the DATAX0 register (0x32) for the X, Y, Z axis data every 100 ms, and converts the raw signed 16-bit values to g-force using a scale factor of 256 LSB/g. A freefall event is detected when all three axes have an absolute value below 0.2g for a continuous 0.5 seconds, confirmed by reading twice with a 0.5 second delay. On a confirmed freefall, the GPIO27 pin is driven high to simulate an alarm, held for 5 seconds, then set low. The freefall event is logged to freefall.log in CSV format with a timestamp (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS) and x, y, z values to 3 decimal places. I2C errors are handled by printing to stderr and continuing operation, checking every pigpio and I2C call. A SIGINT handler is used to close the I2C handle, set GPIO low, and terminate pigpio.

