### Explanation:
This is a complete, compilable C program that subscribes to the MQTT topic home/lights/control via the libmosquitto client library and controls a relay module on GPIO17 (physical pin 11, BCM) using pigpio.

The program initializes pigpio, configures GPIO17 as an output, and drives it LOW (relay OFF) at startup. It connects to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 with client ID relay_controller_1, clean-session enabled, and a 60-second keepalive, logging every connection, subscription, disconnection, and error event to syslog (facility LOG_USER, tag mqtt_relay).

On a successful connect, the program subscribes to home/lights/control at QoS 0; on failure, it logs the connack string and keeps the process alive for retry. In the message callback, the program treats the payload as a NUL-terminated string: ON sets GPIO17 HIGH (relay energized) and OFF sets it LOW (relay de-energized); it logs every received message, and if the payload is empty or anything other than ON/OFF, it logs an error via syslog(LOG_ERR, ...) and leaves the relay state unchanged.

The program runs mosquitto_loop in the main thread; if it returns an error or the broker disconnects unexpectedly, it destroys the client, waits 5 seconds, and reconnects automatically, never exiting on transient MQTT failures.

The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown: it stops the loop, sets GPIO17 LOW, disconnects and destroys the mosquitto client, calls mosquitto_lib_cleanup(), gpioTerminate(), and closelog().

It checks every pigpio and mosquitto return code and reports errors via syslog.

The program is built with: gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o relay_controller relay_controller.c -lmosquitto -lpigpio -lrt.

