This program demonstrates a robust and efficient solution for controlling a 5V relay using a TTP223 capacitive touch sensor on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. The program uses the pigpio library, implements software debounce, and handles errors gracefully. The program is self-contained and easy to understand, making it a great starting point for anyone looking to control a relay using a capacitive touch sensor on a Raspberry Pi.

