The program uses the libgpiod API, not wiringPi, to access the GPIO. It uses the GPIOD_LINE_REQUEST_FLAG_BIAS_PULL_UP flag to enable the internal pull-up on the line, since the A3144's open-collector output requires a pull-up. It uses edge-triggered event detection (gpiod_line_event_wait) to count pulses, with a 2 ms debounce window to reject contact bounce and double-edge noise.

The program uses the clock_gettime function with CLOCK_MONOTONIC to get the current time, and the strftime and snprintf functions to format the time in ISO 8601 format. It uses the fwrite and fflush functions to write the log entry to the log file, and the printf function to print the current RPM to stdout.

The program handles errors by printing clear diagnostics to stderr and exiting non-zero on failure. It checks the return values of gpiod_chip_open, gpiod_chip_get_line, gpiod_line_request_input_flags, and gpiod_line_request_event_flags, and exits if any of them fail.

