### Conclusion:
This is a complete, compilable C program that uses the pigpio library for UART access, never wiringPi, to interface with a Texas Instruments AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor over /dev/ttyS0 at 921600 baud. It continuously reads the asynchronous TLV byte stream, synchronizes on the 8-byte magic word 0x0204 0x0306 0x0805 0x0709 (little-endian), validates the TLV payload, and extracts each detected object's range and velocity. For each detected object, it writes a row to radar_data.csv with columns timestamp, object_index, range_m, velocity_mps. It checks every UART read, handles partial reads and buffer overflows gracefully, skips malformed frames, and logs errors to stderr without crashing. On all exit paths, including SIGINT and SIGTERM, it closes the UART, flushes and closes the CSV file, and calls gpioTerminate().

