# mmwave-radar-sensor-interface

## Introduction

This repository contains a C program that interfaces with a Texas Instruments AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor. The program uses the pigpio library to access the UART device and read data from the sensor. It then processes the data and writes it to a CSV file.

## Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4
- Texas Instruments AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor
- pigpio library

## Installation

To install the pigpio library, follow the instructions on the [pigpio website](http://abyz.me.uk/rpi/pigpio/).

## Usage

To run the program, connect the UART device to the sensor and run the following command:

```
gcc -Wall -o mmwave mmwave.c -lpigpio -lrt -lpthread
sudo ./mmwave
```

The program will read data from the sensor and write it to a CSV file named `radar_data.csv`.

## Data Format

The data from the sensor is in the following format:

```
timestamp,object_index,range_m,velocity_mps
```

- `timestamp`: The timestamp of the data.
- `object_index`: The index of the object.
- `range_m`: The range of the object in meters.
- `velocity_mps`: The velocity of the object in meters per second.

